&lt;p>There is an old, simple question that can help us understand a fundamental property of the universe. It is usually called Olbers' paradox, after the German astronomer Heinrich Wilhelm Olbers:&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>Why is the night sky dark?&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This short outreach note is preserved in the site archive and is not promoted on the homepage.&lt;/p>
